#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsine"}] :question/id #uuid "f1eb9fd6-8927-54e9-bb01-57dd52871d59" :question/math-academy-id "e-386" :question/problem "Calculate the indefinite integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x = \\arcsin (x) + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}dx &= 3\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}dx \\\\\n&= 3\\arcsin (x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7256d2e-7105-5a4e-8d0a-5e00dfc1e311" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arctangent"}] :question/id #uuid "7a798e77-3c04-51e3-adec-d695724ce450" :question/math-academy-id "e-387" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{2}{1 + x^{2}}dx &= 2\\int\\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= 2\\arctan x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e6b5d85-0b53-580f-9520-6c33463231d5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Inverse Trigonometric Functions and Some Manipulations"}] :question/id #uuid "6ff9c057-e61a-5648-9a49-72a70f3127bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-388" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {x^2+2}{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} + 2}{x^{2} + 1} &= \\frac{x^{2} + 1 + 1}{x^{2} + 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1} \\textrm dx = \\arctan(x)\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{x^{2} + 2}{x^{2} + 1}dx &= \\int(1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1})dx \\\\\n&= \\int1dx + \\int\\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}dx \\\\\n&= x + \\arctan (x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67f41769-a0ff-5ecc-8b05-5890a7ac9fe3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsecant"}] :question/id #uuid "81e3df9e-e5ab-57ec-9a82-149a277e94f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3890" :question/problem "If $f'(x) = \\dfrac{5}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} - 2x$, then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm dx = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, x\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= \\intf^{′}(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\frac{5}{\\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}} - 2x)dx \\\\ = \\int\\frac{5}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx - \\int2xdx \\\\ = 5\\int\\frac{1}{\\mid x\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx - 2\\intxdx \\\\\n&= 5arcsec(x) - 2 \\cdot \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C \\\\\n&= 5arcsec(x) - x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "910ceea0-2132-53dd-8572-be4a025c2ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\arcsin x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061374} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ef5d6c-237c-5dae-9c5e-c20a1bd00eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\arctan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061375} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bde417-11fc-5d8a-b67d-8